License — content in this directory
====================================

Everything under public/content/ is generated by scripts in scripts/ingest/
(see CLAUDE.md — never hand-edit these files directly) and is licensed
separately from the application source code in src/ (see the repo-root
LICENSE for that).

Current status (Phase 1): only kana.json and curriculum.json exist, both
entirely hand-authored (§5.3) — no JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KanjiVG, or Tatoeba
data is in use yet. The licenses below are documented now, ahead of that
content landing in Phase 2, so the obligations are correct and visible
from day one rather than retrofitted later.

Because KANJIDIC2 and KanjiVG are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 / CC BY-SA 3.0
respectively, their share-alike terms require any derivative data files —
including the generated shards in this directory — to also be licensed
CC BY-SA 4.0 or later. Accordingly:

**All content files in public/content/ are licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).**

This directory's content is additionally derived from, and carries
attribution obligations to, the following sources. Full attribution text
is in the repo-root NOTICE file and rendered in-app on the Credits screen.

| Source | License | Provides |
|---|---|---|
| JMdict / JMnedict / Kradfile / Radkfile | EDRDG Licence (https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html) | Word entries, kanji-radical decomposition |
| KANJIDIC2 | CC BY-SA 4.0 | Per-kanji meanings, readings, stroke data |
| KanjiVG | CC BY-SA 3.0 | Stroke-order SVG paths |
| Tatoeba | CC BY 2.0 FR (a subset CC0 1.0) | Example sentences |

The EDRDG licence and CC BY 2.0 FR both require attribution but are not
share-alike in the same way CC BY-SA is — CC BY-SA 4.0 was chosen as the
umbrella license for this directory specifically because it's compatible
with and satisfies all four sources' requirements at once (attribution +
share-alike). If a future content addition is licensed in a way
incompatible with CC BY-SA 4.0, it must not be added to this directory
without revisiting this file.
